top to bottom direction
class "messaging (processing)" as M <<module>> $PROC {
 {static} - _retry_locked(session, job, request_id)
 {static} + emit_state(session, job, attempt)
 {static} + finish(factory, work, *, outputs=None, error=None)
}
class "lifecycle (processing)" as L <<module>> $PROC {
 {static} + lock_pair(session, job_id, attempt_id)
 {static} + db_now(session)
 {static} + live(pair, token, now)
 {static} + heartbeat(factory, work, settings)
 {static} + finish(factory, work, *, outputs=None, error=None, on_change=None)
}
class "recovery (processing)" as R <<module>> $PROC {
 {static} + recover_expired(factory, *, limit=100, on_change=None, job_filter=None)
 {static} + interrupt(session, job, attempt, now, message, on_change=None)
}
M -[hidden]right- R
M ..> L : lock_pair / live
R ..> L : lock_pair / db_now
R ..> M : on_change=emit_state
legend bottom
+ public; - internal by Python convention; underlined = class/module scope.
Real untyped Python signatures. These are not Job methods. All mutations serialize on the Job root lock.
live requires current/nondeleted Job + processing states + matching token + unexpired DB-clock lease/deadline.
